 "speech": {
  "language": "en",
  "text": "is postpartum blues? So postpartum blues usually start after delivery within two to three days of delivery and last up to two weeks. the end before two weeks, usually what happens is the mother feels very emotional, overwhelmed, stressed, cries without any reason. That is usually due to a massive dip in the progesterone and the estrogen levels. It is normal to feel overwhelmed and stressed at that particular time. And it happens in 50 to 70 % women. So there's nothing to worry about. It's normal. But if this lasts beyond more than two weeks, then it is something to worry about then you should consult a psychiatrist.",
